{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1118511-who-what-is-the-greatest-threat-to-the-world-of-darkness","id":1118511,"title":"Who/what is the greatest threat to the World of Darkness?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-20T06:40:26-07:00","id":1118511,"title":"Who/what is the greatest threat to the World of Darkness?","content":"So I know that there have been variations of this question, but specifically, I'm asking what single person or entity is the scariest or most likely to inflcit maximum carnage or devastation effectively? <br /> <br /> To operationally define it further:<br /> <br /> -not an organization or group (e.g., the Technocracy, the Antedeluvians) or vague spiritual concept (e.g., the Wyrm)<br /> <br /> -a specific member of a group (e.g., Lillith, the Unnamed, Belial, Absimiliard)<br /> <br /> -consider not only raw power, but also control, agency, scope of power, plans, intent, weaknesses, etc. (example: Caine certainly is incredibly powerful - assuming the withering hasn't depowered him--but is he overtly malicious? Also, he has some known weaknesses and that all vampires have)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","name":"Trategos_Sol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T08:03:25-07:00","id":1118559,"title":"","content":"The different game lines have different cosmologies and so the answer may vary. <br /> <br /> That said, in at least some cosmologies the Christian version of Satan exists and so it's hard to say that anything is more dangerous than him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T10:07:58-07:00","id":1118598,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Martin Ericsson probably poses the greatest threat to the World of Darkness. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T12:31:54-07:00","id":1118664,"title":"","content":"Ordinary humans .Each supernatural faction has rules that require them not to bother the ordinary humans, for ordinary humans can block reality changes (Mage), hunt down vampires who do not follow the Masquerade (Vampire), are full of Banality (Changeling) and are agents of the Wyrm or Weaver (could be both, but they aren't the Wyld in Werewolf). I don't know enough about Wraith, but I'd assume humans left behind are anchors keeping wraiths from moving on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T13:19:20-07:00","id":1118679,"title":"","content":"Voormas I'd say. He's pretty much the only openly active big bad of the settings (aside from the antedevulians but Im gonna ignore them)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11894-shushu","name":"Shushu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T14:58:16-07:00","id":1118714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shushu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1118511-who-what-is-the-greatest-threat-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1118679#post1118679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Voormas I'd say. He's pretty much the only openly active big bad of the settings (aside from the antedevulians but Im gonna ignore them)</div> </div> </div> </div>This pretty much emphasizes a point that undermines the thread, in that there is no antagonist from another game that other games cannot ignore. Technowhatsits? Voorwho? Antepastos? There's no obligation that makes their presence necessary, and nothing to keep together a unified WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T15:52:28-07:00","id":1118732,"title":"","content":"It would probably have to be one of the specific Malfeans, probably a Neverborn. Each is extremely powerful in its own right. Each has legions of spectres and Nephwrack cults devoted to it. Each, while dreaming, spawns the various masters of the Nephandi and thus controls them. They are specific entities as opposed to a vague spiritual designation like the Wyrm or Oblivion. The question is simply trying to identify a particularly &quot;active&quot; one which afflicts the real, living world. The two best candidates would be either Rabark or Zyras who are named in both Wraith and Orpheus. I don't include Gorool simply because at the present, he's indisposed because of Charon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T15:56:11-07:00","id":1118734,"title":"","content":"Yes, there is nothing like the Great Old Ones to force the various creatures to work together. The Demons of DtF should have honestly been the big bad. They could have been an exploratory force of tens of thousands of alien spiritual entities laying the groundwork for an invasion of millions of their more powerful peers who sought to enslave everyone, but oWW did not really explore that potential metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T16:18:52-07:00","id":1118746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1118511-who-what-is-the-greatest-threat-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1118732#post1118732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would probably have to be one of the specific Malfeans, probably a Neverborn. Each is extremely powerful in its own right. Each has legions of spectres and Nephwrack cults devoted to it. Each, while dreaming, spawns the various masters of the Nephandi and thus controls them. They are specific entities as opposed to a vague spiritual designation like the Wyrm or Oblivion. The question is simply trying to identify a particularly &quot;active&quot; one which afflicts the real, living world. The two best candidates would be either Rabark or Zyras who are named in both Wraith and Orpheus. I don't include Gorool simply because at the present, he's indisposed because of Charon.</div> </div> </div> </div>We had a setting where the Neverborn and their minions were the biggest of big bads, but it eventually turned into one where the Ebon Dragon was duping everyone after all, and then people began to question whether or not we actually needed big bads when there were so many other, more compelling and interesting problems in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T00:40:17-07:00","id":1118858,"title":"","content":"How about the Children that the Baali worshipped? I might be wrong but I always got the impression that if one of those wake up then we're all f*cked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/629-anda","name":"anda","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T07:20:15-07:00","id":1118945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This pretty much emphasizes a point that undermines the thread, in that there is no antagonist from another game that other games cannot ignore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, there cannot exist a &quot;greatest antagonist&quot; because there isn't a unified cosmology where one can gauge the existential threath someone posesses.<br /> <br /> If someone were to say &quot;The Great Old Ones&quot; one will have the right to ask &quot;What Great Old Ones?&quot;: That Head of the Wyrm that tried to materialize and would have devoured earth if wasn't for Croatan's sacrifice?, Belial?, A Neverborn?, Shaitan's master Namataru?, one of the Children?, The Devil (but not Lucifer, he's a good guy)?, One of the other umbral masters that the Nephandy serve?, a creature of the Deep Umbra like Lakleeb the Lightless?, a Fomorian?.<br /> <br /> The Unnamed and Voormas have each one an End World scenario in Mage where they fuck up the whole universe with very little help, that makes them very dangerous, but aren't mentioned elsewhere, thus their danger it's meaningless in other settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-21-2017, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T16:11:51-07:00","id":1119101,"title":"","content":"<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>God45.</li> <li>Me.</li> <li>Your mother.</li> <li>The squirrel spying on you through the window right no<b>DON'T LOOK! He'll know you're on to him!</b></li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"us