/> 4 - Has the power to reshape the flesh and bone of other life forms at will, transforming them into monstrous abominations bound to its command.<br /> <br /> <br /> If / when they ever decide to take action, they could absorb the entire city's population and unleash an army of millions of Vohzd upon the world!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-22-2017, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T16:29:28-07:00","id":1119360,"title":"","content":"Bad Writing! <br /> Ok, sorry, reflex, let me be more nuanced<br /> POWERGAMERS!<br /> As soon as something has stats, they manage to kill it! It's insane!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T17:14:53-07:00","id":1119365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Davesknd</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">POWERGAMERS!<br /> As soon as something has stats, they manage to kill it! It's insane!</div> </div> </div> </div>Evil Storytellers aren't even bound by that limitation, they easily narrate God's defeat at the hands of her new pet character before ending WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T19:04:04-07:00","id":1119381,"title":"","content":"I always think that a ST should make sure that things are not that easy for the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T09:45:24-07:00","id":1119548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1118511-who-what-is-the-greatest-threat-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1119312#post1119312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4 - Has the power to reshape the flesh and bone of other life forms at will, transforming them into monstrous abominations bound to its command.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worse than you think. Because Auspex is one of the clan's affinity disciplines, it means it also has it at level 10/plot device, and one of the things you can do with Auspex at that level is use touch range powers anywhere you can project your mind to. So the Eldest can actually warp, twist, fold and mutilate the body of anyone on the planet<i> just by thinking about it</i>. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T11:06:13-07:00","id":1119957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1118511-who-what-is-the-greatest-threat-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1119365#post1119365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Evil Storytellers aren't even bound by that limitation, they easily narrate God's defeat at the hands of her new pet character before ending WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded! When the storyteller is a powergamer and his girlfriend plays his pet PC, you're gonna have a bad time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T14:29:45-07:00","id":1124008,"title":"","content":"The Tzimisce Antediluvian, at least in part. Last I checked, he was out to infect the Earth and subsume Gaia. Basically, if he gets far enough, he'd basically do the Wym's job for it, assuming he ISN&quot;T the Wyrm, at least some aspect of it. His origin is FUCKED UP, depending on which version you go with. (One basically says he's the Dark Side of some 2nd Gen (or Saulot) that took on humanoid vampire form after it purged himself to allow for greater wisdom).<br /> <br /> Ravana fought off 3 bodhisattva, and every werewolf who could show up to fight near Bangladesh, and tht Technos STILL had to nuke his ass with special magic nukes, and even THAT didn't kill him. It took the Bodhisattva lifting the monsoon raging to allow the Technos to hit him with the reflection of multiple suns thanks to special technomagick satellites. And I'm pretty sure THAT only worked because Ravy was running on Empty as he'd just woken up and had been fighting a week-long running battle through the jungles of Southeast Asia.<br /> <br /> What weapon are you going to pull out against something that's basically infected the planet itself and no longer has a physical body to attack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T14:53:28-07:00","id":1124018,"title":"","content":"Well prior to the gehenna novels you had a Methuselah in D.C with his finger next to the button with plans to nuke his rivals and rebuild humanity after the fallout clears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T21:44:32-07:00","id":1124171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1118511-who-what-is-the-greatest-threat-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1124018#post1124018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well prior to the gehenna novels you had a Methuselah in D.C with his finger next to the button with plans to nuke his rivals and rebuild humanity after the fallout clears.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;This nuclear war plan is awesome! All I have to do is exert some pressure on the remnants of humanity... while subsisting on blood taken from younger vampires, who take it from the vastly decreased and scattered remnants of humanity...&quot;<br /> <br /> (Beat)<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, you know what, this plan sucks. It's as bad as those wackos who want to blot out the sun.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T14:24:27-07:00","id":1124479,"title":"","content":"If you go with the idea of Saulot attempting to become the Demon Emperor, then Saulot would be the greatest threat to oWoD. As the Demon Emperor, he would be able to loose millions of demons and billions of damned souls upon the Earth, as well as commanding the Demon Lords and Akuma of the 1,000 Hells. It would make Ravnos look like a temper tantrum of a 2 year old by comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T18:00:41-07:00","id":1124551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1118511-who-what-is-the-greatest-threat-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1124479#post1124479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you go with the idea of Saulot attempting to become the Demon Emperor, then Saulot would be the greatest threat to oWoD. As the Demon Emperor, he would be able to loose millions of demons and billions of damned souls upon the Earth, as well as commanding the Demon Lords and Akuma of the 1,000 Hells. It would make Ravnos look like a temper tantrum of a 2 year old by comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternately, if Haight had continued to snowball in significance and ridiculousness instead of being written out, he might have ended up in a &quot;threat to everyone&quot; capacity beyond that of The Chaos Factor. Thankfully, he was written into a soulsteel ashtray instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T17:27:34-07:00","id":1126113,"title":"","content":"Haight makes a good threat to the World of Darkness as a meta-threat to the game lines too, representing a sort of edgy-cool powergaming twinkery that would have driven customers away in droves if it had continued to be White Wolf's guiding tone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T10:16:27-07:00","id":1126346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1118511-who-what-is-the-greatest-threat-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1126113#post1126113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haight makes a good threat to the World of Darkness as a meta-threat to the game lines too, representing a sort of edgy-cool powergaming twinkery <b>that would have driven customers away in droves if it had continued to be White Wolf's guiding tone</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's interesting. Since I'm someone who actually enjoys that type of tone and 90's edge(God, I hate that fucking word).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T10:29:03-07:00","id":1126762,"title":"","content":"Haight was a bad joke, but it would be nice if there were threats that would unify the desperate factions of cWoD. Pentex could potentially work as one because it has something to hate for every 'good' faction of the six majors. It works with the Wyrm, so the Fera hate it. It works with the Sabbat, so the Camarilla hates it. It works with the Unseelie, so the Seelie hate it. It works with the Technocracy, so the Traditions hate it. It works with the Specters, so Wraiths hate it. It works with the Demon Lords, so the KJ hate it. In that vein, I think that Pentex could and should be a universal threat in cWoD, regardless of the type of supernatural creature involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T11:48:38-07:00","id":1126791,"title":"","content":"Exalted Player Characters and a Time Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T14:07:32-07:00","id":1126842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1118511-who-what-is-the-greatest-threat-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1126762#post1126762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haight was a bad joke, but it would be nice if there were threats that would unify the desperate factions of cWoD. Pentex could potentially work as one because it has something to hate for every 'good' faction of the six majors. It works with the Wyrm, so the Fera hate it. It works with the Sabbat, so the Camarilla hates it. It works with the Unseelie, so the Seelie hate it. It works with the Technocracy, so the Traditions hate it. It works with the Specters, so Wraiths hate it. It works with the Demon Lords, so the KJ hate it. In that vein, I think that Pentex could and should be a universal threat in cWoD, regardless of the type of supernatural creature involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem being that it's a hands-off shell company that works through deniability and is not the only thing of its kind, so it has a good deal of camouflage, or should, to protect it from the harsh light of discovery. Also, why would the Cam hate it? They can both make huge amounts of money investing in it, just like Enzo Giovanni did. It's not like they advertise &quot;COOL SABBAT CLUB!&quot; or the like, or actually follow Zettler's beliefs. I doubt that the Gui Ren care much about it, either, except for the Resplendent Cranes, and that's because a large number of the Cranes are all about &quot;destroy all the tendrils of the White Ghost-Devils!&quot; rather than any specific beef that they might have with Pentex.<br /> <br /> Finally, per C20, I think that most Unseelie steer away from it, since Unseelie doesn't mean EEEEEVIL! Even the Thallain of the Shadow Court are going to be wary of them, because Pentex's operations are pretty much Banality squared. It starts with TPS report cover sheets, and then gets more boring from there on in. That's another part of their camouflage, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T16:16:44-07:00","id":1126871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1118511-who-what-is-the-greatest-threat-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1124171#post1124171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;This nuclear war plan is awesome! All I have to do is exert some pressure on the remnants of humanity... while subsisting on blood taken from younger vampires, who take it from the vastly decreased and scattered remnants of humanity...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNever said it was a good plan.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T00:23:24-07:00","id":1127955,"title":"","content":"BAD FANFICTION AND BAD DMS!<br /> <br /> <br /> That..and possibly Grandmaw or Humanity Itself","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T19:22:04-07:00","id":1128305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1118511-who-what-is-the-greatest-threat-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1124171#post1124171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;This nuclear war plan is awesome! All I have to do is exert some pressure on the remnants of humanity... while subsisting on blood taken from younger vampires, who take it from the vastly decreased and scattered remnants of humanity...&quot;<br /> <br /> (Beat)<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, you know what, this plan sucks. It's as bad as those wackos who want to blot out the sun.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Realistically thinking, would the nations of the world really decide to launch their nukes all over the fucking planet just because somebody fired upon another country?<br /> <br /> I feel like that would be an extreme over reaction to the situation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah, I stand by my city sized, Lovecraftian vampire god who, as others pointed out, can turn people into Chaos Spawn with a mere thought.<br /> <br /> And, oh yeah, there's the fact that Vicisitude can reconstitute your body from Final Death (ashes), thereby making you <b>completely immortal.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-12-2017, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T19:26:22-07:00","id":1128307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1118511-who-what-is-the-greatest-threat-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1128305#post1128305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Realistically thinking, would the nations of the world really decide to launch their nukes all over the fucking planet just because somebody fired upon another country?<br /> <br /> I feel like that would be an extreme over reaction to the situation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah, I stand by my city sized, Lovecraftian vampire god who, as others pointed out, can turn people into Chaos Spawn with a mere thought.<br /> <br /> And, oh yeah, there's the fact that Vicisitude can reconstitute your body from Final Death (ashes), thereby making you <b>completely immortal.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>What's that? An Ultimate Being throwing its weight around, you say? <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xAXIbYI9RgU\" target=\"_blank\">There's a solution for that...</a> (spoilers for JoJo series 2)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 08-12-2017, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T19:35:04-07:00","id":1128309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1118511-who-what-is-the-greatest-threat-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1128307#post1128307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's that? An Ultimate Being throwing its weight around, you say? <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xAXIbYI9RgU\" target=\"_blank\">There's a solution for that...</a> (spoilers for JoJo series 2)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Good luck feasibly replicating the feat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T23:53:09-07:00","id":1128347,"title":"","content":"Isn't there a Lasombra Elder ritual that envelops wide areas in a black portal to a world devoid of flesh and elements?...because if that isn't capable of consuming a city wide area I'm sure Lasombra has something that can...Ya know, the god that fused himself with the primordial darkness that existed before creation to become even more powerful, that one...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T07:05:35-07:00","id":1128430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1118511-who-what-is-the-greatest-threat-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1128309#post1128309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Good luck feasibly replicating the feat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Given the greater ease of being able to produce volcanic eruptions, you don't need much luck...<br /> <br /> Your next post will be, &quot;But Antediluvians could control that, too! You have no hope of defeating them!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T08:47:43-07:00","id":1128467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1118511-who-what-is-the-greatest-threat-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1128430#post1128430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given the greater ease of being able to produce volcanic eruptions, you don't need much luck...<br /> <br /> Your next post will be, &quot;But Antediluvians could control that, too! You have no hope of defeating them!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But Antediluvians could control that, too! You have no hope of defeating them!</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Actually, I was more curious about the amount of force required to jettison an <b>entire city</b> into outer space.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And then there's Saulot, an Ante who's been secretly manipulating an entire clan to keep knowledge of Thaumaturgy out of the hands of anybody else. Essentially meaning that when Saulot decides to make his move, he has access to an entire discipline's worth of power that nobody else knows the limits of. There's no contingency plan in place to stop him, because the contingency plan works for him!<br /> <br /> And considering Thaumataturgy in the past has been shown to curse entire lineages, or even wipe them out of existence without any prior warning, we can say without bias that Saulot is nigh omnipotent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T12:21:53-07:00","id":1128541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And then there's Saulot, an Ante who's been <b>secretly manipulating an entire clan to keep knowledge of Thaumaturgy out of the hands of anybody else</b>. Essentially meaning that when Saulot decides to make his move, he has access to an entire discipline's worth of power that nobody else knows the limits of. There's no contingency plan in place to stop him, because the contingency plan works for him!</div> </div> </div> </div>And he has been failing misserably at that!, if we take in count the amount of schools of Blood Magic, the fact that every clan has Matusalems with Thaum-like powers, Independent clans have entire factions with it, there are also high level practicioners within every sect that isn't the Camarilla, and the fact that Tzimisce has, likely, Koldunism at 10 thanks to Kupala.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T13:36:39-07:00","id":1128565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I was more curious about the amount of force required to jettison an <b>entire city</b> into outer space.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder...New York has a smaller area than many volcanic eruptions, and Tzimi being of flesh and bone it's likely lighter than a city, but the problem it's to make him break the atmosphere and in one piece to boot. I think the eruption would likely turn him to ash and disperse his body trough the atmosphere, which won't kill him, but would effectively remove Tzimi from the Gehena party, giving other Antes time to win. Alternatively you could create a breach in earth's crust wide enough to hurl Tzimisce to the moltern center of earth where he's going to spend eternity being turned into ash (or eaten by Ennoia). You just need to ask a Forces Archmage to break the local tectonic plaque in the correct place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T14:24:02-07:00","id":1128575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1118511-who-what-is-the-greatest-threat-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1128541#post1128541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And he has been failing misserably at that!, if we take in count the amount of schools of Blood Magic, the fact that every clan has Matusalems with Thaum-like powers, Independent clans have entire factions with it, there are also high level practicioners within every sect that isn't the Camarilla, and the fact that Tzimisce has, likely, Koldunism at 10 thanks to Kupala.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From what I've read about it, Thaumaturgy isn't the same thing as general blood magic. It's a Path of blood magic that approaches its research from a scientific lens. The other paths use philosophy, mysticism, or even religion to accomplish their rituals, but the Tremere version approaches it with secular rationalism.<br /> <br /> Again, this is only what I've been able to read about it. So if anybody has a more accurate description, feel free to correct me.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for dispersing Tzimi across the atmosphere, I think we should call John Carpenter about that. Because I not want bits and pieces of a (possible) alien parasite floating around my breathing space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T06:24:21-07:00","id":1128780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I've read about it, Thaumaturgy isn't the same thing as general blood magic. It's a Path of blood magic that approaches its research from a scientific lens. The other paths use philosophy, mysticism, or even religion to accomplish their rituals, but the Tremere version approaches it with secular rationalism.<br /> <br /> Again, this is only what I've been able to read about it. So if anybody has a more accurate description, feel free to correct me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have one: Thaumaturgy and at least half of the other blood magic share all the same Paths and Rituals, thus they're the same. Different approach, same power. You cannot say &quot;Aha!, I have Thaumaturgy a rare and unique power, you will never expect what my rituals can do!&quot; when Assamites can either use or develop the same Path/Rituals. Just see how &quot;surprised&quot; was Ur-Shulgi when he awoke and found his clan under a Thaumaturgical curse, he was so surprised by the &quot; unknown powers&quot; of the Coucil of Seven's curse that he obliterated it effortlessly.<br /> <br /> Koldun stuff and Necromancy are the only &quot;blood magics&quot; that can be said to be trully different (as in, they don't share the same Paths/Rituals). Assamite mojo has all the same powers but with a more flexible approach, Setite mojo has the same powers and then some, Inconnu has blood magic that works just like Thaum, Anarch stuff it's derived from Thaum, The Sabbat still teaches the Thaum that antitribu tremere brought with them before being destroyed.<br /> <br /> Thus, if preventing others from having Thaumaturgy was Saulot's plan...he didn't do a good job.<br /> <br /> ...on the other hand, Saulot it's rumored to be Baali Antediluvian. Having Daimonion, Thaumaturgy and whole clans of demonologists and mages may come in hand when your plan it's to become the demon king of the sixth age.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for dispersing Tzimi across the atmosphere, I think we should call John Carpenter about that. Because I not want bits and pieces of a (possible) alien parasite floating around my breathing space. </div> </div> </div>Indeed. I wonder how much Tzimisce it's needed to co-opt another Antediluvian's body, albeit I imagine some, like Lasombra, are immune on the grounds of not having flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-14-2017, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T07:08:45-07:00","id":1129769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1118511-who-what-is-the-greatest-threat-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1126113#post1126113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haight makes a good threat to the World of Darkness as a meta-threat to the game lines too, representing a sort of edgy-cool powergaming twinkery that would have driven customers away in droves if it had continued to be White Wolf's guiding tone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haight was a good idea, executed *badly*. They basically tried wayyyy to hard to make him the ultimate badass, with access to *everything*. They also ramrodded him down everyone' throat every other module, as I recall. <br /> <br /> I came up with a version that was a Tremere experiment that went horribly wrong/right (point of view). Basically, take a Metis Shadow Lord Garou, Embraced thaumaturigically into the Embrace, using a bastardization of the ritual they used to become vampires in the first place. (They were trying to see if by taking Garou traits into themselves, if they could alleviate the condition somewhat). It worked, but he was a monster. He escaped before he could be put down. <br /> <br /> I came up with a new Abomination template to make him truly horrifying, rather than pathetic, like RAW insists they be, compensated for it, by making procreation nigh-impossible, and his &quot;magic&quot; is simply the fact that as a Tremere bloodline, he has Thaumaturgy as In-Clan Discipline, rather than coming up with some bullshit workaround to fake doing True Magick. His modus operandi is to stay in the shadows, because he's the most hunted creature on the planet, and his goal is reverse-engineer his creation ritual to make more like himself. He's a metaplot bogeyman, like the Niktuku, rather than this recurring villain the original metaplot had him as.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T08:17:40-07:00","id":1129795,"title":"","content":"Abominations have a route that allows them to not be pathetic, it is to go into service to the Wyrm. It is only by trying to remain true to Gaia that Abominations suffer, as the Gnosis of Gaia is effectively a poison to any Kindred without the protections of the Wyrm, which is probably why the vast majority of Abominations commit suicide in spectacular fashion. Death is a better fate than service to the Wyrm, so death is a better fate than to remain an Abomination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T10:29:14-07:00","id":1132277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1118511-who-what-is-the-greatest-threat-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1129795#post1129795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abominations have a route that allows them to not be pathetic, it is to go into service to the Wyrm. It is only by trying to remain true to Gaia that Abominations suffer, as the Gnosis of Gaia is effectively a poison to any Kindred without the protections of the Wyrm, which is probably why the vast majority of Abominations commit suicide in spectacular fashion. Death is a better fate than service to the Wyrm, so death is a better fate than to remain an Abomination.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not why abominations are in harano. Abominations are in permanent harano because being a vampire sucks and it is contrary to their nature as Garou. It's not that Gnosis is a poison. Gnosis isn't the problem, vampirism is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T00:14:59-07:00","id":1133689,"title":"","content":"It might be Nightmaster, He can erase the world or change it in very unkind way in Shattered Dreams. The same character is mastermind behind extermination of Nuwisha in one of Apocalypse scenarios and that started the last battle ... of course Grand Maw from Orpheus, Caine (I always think that he is Eater of Souls, Wyrm aspect). The top 3 for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T09:52:54-07:00","id":1134859,"title":"","content":"Greatest threat?<br /> <br /> Apathy...................meh","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 09-01-2017, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T03:11:17-07:00","id":1136125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1118511-who-what-is-the-greatest-threat-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1129795#post1129795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abominations have a route that allows them to not be pathetic, it is to go into service to the Wyrm. It is only by trying to remain true to Gaia that Abominations suffer, as the Gnosis of Gaia is effectively a poison to any Kindred without the protections of the Wyrm, which is probably why the vast majority of Abominations commit suicide in spectacular fashion. Death is a better fate than service to the Wyrm, so death is a better fate than to remain an Abomination.</div> </div> </div> </div>They also have a few DM fiat open ends thatwhite wolf never closed. Like interaction between diablerie and harano(a wolf addicted to diablerie because it temerarily relieves harano sounds like a good NPC character), also how blood magic + gifts work(new &quot;blood&quot; gifts and powers like the liannan's ogham discipline), and if golconda frees a werewolf from the ever spiraling gnosis problem.<br /> <br /> Though Abominations aren't as powerful as a bain/weaver spirit possessed vampire if you use the &quot;Possessed&quot; sourcebook from werewolf. Having a possessing spirit giving you werewolf rage, gnosis, regeneration, a war form, and gifts without ever worrying about decaying gnosis AND you get bonus powers garou will never have. It also fits the story to have a bain possessed(or &quot;possessed&quot; thaumaturgists can force it if necessary) vamp being a major threat to both werewolves and vampires can be the reason for a team up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 09-01-2017, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T23:05:19-07:00","id":1136499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1118511-who-what-is-the-greatest-threat-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1129795#post1129795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abominations have a route that allows them to not be pathetic, it is to go into service to the Wyrm. It is only by trying to remain true to Gaia that Abominations suffer, as the Gnosis of Gaia is effectively a poison to any Kindred without the protections of the Wyrm, which is probably why the vast majority of Abominations commit suicide in spectacular fashion. Death is a better fate than service to the Wyrm, so death is a better fate than to remain an Abomination.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about seeking Golconda?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T07:12:19-07:00","id":1136584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1118511-who-what-is-the-greatest-threat-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1136499#post1136499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about seeking Golconda?</div> </div> </div> </div>Never addressed. There are only a handful of Abominations (like 6 at most?) and so the possibly non-existent Golconda route to escape Harano (also a rare-ish state) was never explored. If you think it should cure Harano for your game and you want to go that route, do it. Makes as much sense as anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T23:03:11-07:00","id":1139644,"title":"","content":"With regards to the threat of the Tzimisce Antediluvian, doesn't some fluff suggest that he basically lives lurking in the blood of all his progeny, which is why Vicissitude is looked at with a wary eye? If I'm remembering right, there's a whole concern that the Eldest could basically make puppets of any descendants of his (including the Tremere, ironically). So on top of all of his other insane powers, he could basically have two Clans doing his bidding when it's time to bring about Gehenna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13249-sandcarlyle","name":"SandCarlyle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}